summary: Fuzz keylime TPM quote and TPM2B structure parsing (keylime#1139)
description: |
    Fuzzer test for the hand-written binary parsers in keylime that consume
    data originating from a potentially compromised agent, the highest-priority
    fuzzing target identified in keylime/keylime#1139:

      * tpm2_objects.unmarshal_tpms_attest()  - TPMS_ATTEST quote blob
      * tpm2_objects.pubkey_from_tpm2b_public() - TPM2B_PUBLIC key structure
      * tpm_main.Tpm._get_quote_parameters()  - quote string (base64 + zlib)

    These are manual offset walkers with input-controlled lengths and 32-bit
    loop counts, so the test specifically hunts for crashes, uncaught exception
    types, hangs (input-controlled loop counts -> CPU DoS) and memory
    exhaustion (TPM2B length fields, zlib decompression bombs).

    The test runs in two layers. A deterministic replayer feeds a generated
    corpus of valid and known-adversarial blobs through each parser under a
    wall-clock timeout and requires every input to be rejected gracefully and
    quickly; this needs only the installed keylime package and runs on every
    platform. When atheris (coverage-guided, libFuzzer-backed) can be imported
    or pip-installed, a bounded coverage-guided campaign is run on top, seeded
    from the same corpus; any reproducer atheris saves fails the test and is
    attached to the results.

    Campaign budgets can be raised for longer local runs via the
    FUZZ_MAX_TOTAL_TIME, FUZZ_TIMEOUT and FUZZ_RSS_MB environment variables.
contact: Karel Srot <ksrot@redhat.com>
component:
  - keylime
test: ./test.sh
framework: beakerlib
tag:
  - fuzzing
require:
  - python3
  - python3-pip
  - python3-cryptography
recommend:
  - keylime
  - clang
  - python3-devel
  # keylime already requires these (unconditional imports in signing.py and
  # ima_dm.py), but the quote_params target imports tpm_main.Tpm, which pulls
  # them in transitively; listing them keeps that target from silently
  # degrading to a no-op if keylime's dependency chain ever changes.
  - python3-gpg
  - python3-lark
duration: 15m
enabled: true
id: 6c9d2bd3-4914-411e-932b-6c87997df526
